# Run r1102, SQ-CDJ5 Boot 3: no OUT/srv/miners_upstream (README Boot 3: rm the srv symlink only, never the instance
# folder). The boot is EXPECTED TO STOP in mod construction, so this file sends no console command; it only reads
# logs/latest.log and the crash report.
# Runner: start the boot, then wait for any of: 'reads its textures' in logs/latest.log, a new file in crash-reports/,
# 'Done (' (= FAIL: no stop), with a timeout of about 240 s (Monitor, not sleep loops). After an FML stop the JVM can
# stay alive: kill your recorded pid once the message is in the log (gotchas.md "Boot"), wait for game_jvms.sh to be
# empty, then `qrun.py run OUT b3_nodonor.qb RES`. A boot that never reaches the message nor Done within the timeout:
# kill the pid, keep the log tail in the run notes, the row FAILs on its own (no message line).
